WEBVTT

00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:13.270
Bonsoir, mademoiselle.

00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:17.370
To you, that staff is nothing more

00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:20.240
than a nice little stick that
shoots off fireworks.

00:00:21.190 --> 00:00:23.110
That crossed the line.

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:27.160
Give me the staff.

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:28.250
I refuse.

00:00:28.610 --> 00:00:30.490
Y-Yumiko-chan...

00:00:30.490 --> 00:00:33.800
Be at ease. This is my fight.

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:34.740
Huh?

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:39.730
We can both see each
other's Codes.

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:42.170
There should be no way to run.

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:44.670
In that case, I shall
stand steadfast.

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:46.370
Oh, really?

00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:51.080
Let us settle our differences
atop that building.

00:00:54.770 --> 00:00:57.820
Sounds good. It'll put an
end to this game of tag.

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:00.910
I'll be seeing you, then.

00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:11.300
Yumiko-chan.

00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:19.070
That makes sense. I guess
I am the older one here.

00:01:19.610 --> 00:01:20.710
Are you okay?

00:01:20.710 --> 00:01:22.040
Let's go together.

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:24.450
If we work together, we'll
figure out something.

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:25.350
Okay?

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:33.970
It's Misa-san.

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:35.400
I'll see you later.

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:36.410
But...

00:01:37.460 --> 00:01:39.350
I'll be fine.

00:01:39.560 --> 00:01:44.370
Do what you have to do. You're
going back to the future, right?

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:46.070
But... But...

00:01:46.390 --> 00:01:49.700
I will never give Guibarthez
this staff.

00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:51.420
I promise you.

00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:53.360
Yumiko-chan...

00:01:54.430 --> 00:01:56.520
Six years from now,
let's meet again.

00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:06.220
Look at me! Father! Mother!

00:04:14.660 --> 00:04:16.980
Go on it with me next
time, Father.

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:19.760
Adults can't ride it.

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:21.600
Really?

00:04:22.830 --> 00:04:26.110
It'd be nice if there were other
kids you could play with.

00:04:26.110 --> 00:04:29.840
No! I don't want them
to stare at my hair!

00:04:29.840 --> 00:04:33.180
You're enough for me,
Mother and Father.

00:04:33.490 --> 00:04:34.820
Yumiko.

00:04:43.990 --> 00:04:49.390
I wonder what Mother and Father
said to me back then.

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:53.270
I see. An amusement park...

00:04:54.690 --> 00:04:57.510
Quite a fitting place
for a child to die.

00:04:59.580 --> 00:05:02.230
I think that would apply
to you instead.

00:05:02.620 --> 00:05:04.850
At least you speak
like a grown-up.

00:05:04.850 --> 00:05:06.740
Then I guess I won't hold back.

00:05:07.130 --> 00:05:10.260
Before that, may I ask
you something?

00:05:10.260 --> 00:05:11.250
What is it?

00:05:11.510 --> 00:05:18.640
Which do you think is the strongest: the elephant,
the hunter, or the American president?

00:05:20.440 --> 00:05:21.940
Ta-dah!

00:05:22.990 --> 00:05:27.600
If you stand on top of this and erase the
Christmas Shopper's excess Code,

00:05:27.600 --> 00:05:29.220
everything will be all over.

00:05:29.560 --> 00:05:30.660
Okay...

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:35.240
You'll be able to return to
six years in the future.

00:05:35.240 --> 00:05:37.570
Come on, smile a bit more.

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:43.050
My sister made something weird,
and you're going to stand on it.

00:05:43.050 --> 00:05:45.750
Not to mention the way she talked
about six years from now...

00:05:45.750 --> 00:05:47.920
Everyone here is just...

00:05:48.170 --> 00:05:50.060
Nuts?

00:05:52.110 --> 00:05:55.150
Nuts... Yeah.

00:05:56.150 --> 00:05:57.650
That's pretty apt.

00:06:00.710 --> 00:06:02.590
So, what are you doing?

00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:04.840
You'll stand on this, right?

00:06:04.840 --> 00:06:08.360
I left Yumiko-chan behind.

00:06:08.360 --> 00:06:10.100
That was a wise decision.

00:06:10.100 --> 00:06:13.970
Um... Um... Please
save Yumiko-chan!

00:06:13.970 --> 00:06:15.100
At this rate...

00:06:15.620 --> 00:06:18.110
You have nothing to
do with this world.

00:06:22.030 --> 00:06:23.930
I'll be fine.

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:27.230
Do what you have to do.

00:06:29.440 --> 00:06:31.770
I'm sorry. I have to...

00:06:31.770 --> 00:06:32.990
H-Hey!

00:06:37.020 --> 00:06:39.480
What's with her?

00:06:40.340 --> 00:06:46.000
If this were before I learned magic, I'd have been
so scared, I would have run away! But...

00:06:47.630 --> 00:06:52.000
A mage is the elephant, not
the hunter or the president.

00:06:52.230 --> 00:06:55.670
Magic is power, mademoiselle.

00:06:55.670 --> 00:06:59.850
It's pure power, and power
is destruction.

00:06:59.850 --> 00:07:04.030
Even the elephant's playful actions
can easily kill a human.

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:08.920
In a civilized society, if you want some
water, you just turn a faucet.

00:07:08.920 --> 00:07:13.030
It's something tens of millions
of hands made possible.

00:07:13.260 --> 00:07:16.260
But mages are different.

00:07:16.260 --> 00:07:20.040
Through the power of magic, you could
have it without the help of others.

00:07:20.660 --> 00:07:23.910
You can obtain everything
you desire.

00:07:24.310 --> 00:07:26.910
It's the ultimate existence that stands above all.

00:07:27.830 --> 00:07:30.630
That must have been my
great-grandfather.

00:07:31.180 --> 00:07:36.280
I feel kind of like I understand
what he was trying to say.

00:07:40.190 --> 00:07:42.020
What are you doing?!

00:07:44.420 --> 00:07:45.350
Stop it!

00:07:45.350 --> 00:07:49.610
That's the Sorceress's Library! Those who acquire
it can do as they please with the world!

00:07:51.370 --> 00:07:54.850
My name is Ichinose
Yumiko Cristina.

00:07:54.850 --> 00:07:57.110
The world is already mine!

00:08:03.920 --> 00:08:05.790
I'm finally here.

00:08:14.100 --> 00:08:18.390
Fool, did you think that
would break Kerykeion?

00:08:27.330 --> 00:08:30.660
The Sorceress's Library
is within this.

00:08:35.010 --> 00:08:36.620
Let go.

00:08:36.620 --> 00:08:37.940
Brat!

00:08:43.950 --> 00:08:47.510
Transform to swords, my Code!

00:08:51.350 --> 00:08:52.830
I see.

00:08:52.830 --> 00:08:56.350
The Code is much more precisely
constructed since last I saw it.

00:08:56.350 --> 00:08:57.600
But...

00:08:59.770 --> 00:09:02.740
I told you that magic
was power, did I not?

00:09:11.650 --> 00:09:13.370
You can watch from there

00:09:13.680 --> 00:09:17.380
and witness the moment I obtain
the Sorceress's Library.

00:09:20.520 --> 00:09:24.720
It looks like I won't be able
to keep that promise.

00:09:26.360 --> 00:09:30.770
I wonder if she was able
to make it back safely...

00:09:32.700 --> 00:09:35.130
Are you okay, Yumiko-chan?

00:09:35.670 --> 00:09:37.350
I'm fine.

00:09:38.760 --> 00:09:41.350
That's good! You're up again.

00:09:46.890 --> 00:09:49.060
What are you doing?!

00:09:49.060 --> 00:09:52.770
Well, you can't do
this by yourself!

00:09:52.770 --> 00:09:55.560
What if you can't get back?!

00:09:55.560 --> 00:09:57.220
It'll be okay.

00:09:57.220 --> 00:10:00.030
The Misa-san six years from
now will do something.

00:10:00.030 --> 00:10:02.200
I'll be able to go right back!

00:10:02.480 --> 00:10:05.400
Let's do our best to
recover the staff.

00:10:05.400 --> 00:10:06.280
Okay?

00:10:07.660 --> 00:10:11.030
You're... You're...

00:10:23.540 --> 00:10:24.990
Th-That's...

00:10:33.510 --> 00:10:34.970
Yumiko-chan.

00:10:37.140 --> 00:10:40.470
Those are ghostscripts.

00:10:47.840 --> 00:10:49.730
It's done!

00:10:49.730 --> 00:10:50.990
What's that?

00:10:50.990 --> 00:10:52.000
An amulet.

00:10:52.490 --> 00:10:57.940
The silicon inside will construct 2048
different variable Codes for me.

00:10:57.940 --> 00:11:00.180
It's a required item in
Modern-Day Magic.

00:11:00.800 --> 00:11:06.000
Okay, Santa's gotta give
everyone a present.

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:07.690
See ya.

00:11:09.010 --> 00:11:11.680
Jeez, she's completely nuts.

00:11:19.670 --> 00:11:22.110
Transform to swords, my Code.

00:11:33.790 --> 00:11:35.960
Yumiko-chan, you're bleeding!

00:11:36.360 --> 00:11:39.870
The future Yumiko-chan told me that
if you construct too many Codes,

00:11:39.870 --> 00:11:41.640
your capillaries will rupture.

00:11:41.640 --> 00:11:45.110
In other words, even
magic has a limit.

00:12:02.850 --> 00:12:05.700
There's no choice.
I have to attack.

00:12:05.700 --> 00:12:06.540
Okay!

00:12:08.630 --> 00:12:10.670
Stay in here.

00:12:14.660 --> 00:12:16.400
Here I go.

00:12:23.080 --> 00:12:26.310
It's scary, isn't it? I'm
really scared, too.

00:12:27.710 --> 00:12:32.120
You can change any Code
into a wash basin, right?

00:12:32.120 --> 00:12:33.170
Yeah.

00:12:33.170 --> 00:12:35.680
Even the Sorceress's Library?

00:12:35.680 --> 00:12:38.830
I don't really get it,
but I think I can.

00:12:38.830 --> 00:12:42.810
Then I'll be the bait. You attack.

00:12:42.810 --> 00:12:47.720
You'll end up being the one most
at risk, but is that okay?

00:12:48.520 --> 00:12:53.700
I'll be fine. I thought the two
of us would end up like this.

00:13:16.990 --> 00:13:21.720
Now that I have gained the library,
I have no need for Kerykeion.

00:13:21.720 --> 00:13:26.450
But I shall have the relatives of Cristbarth
and Anehara die here.

00:13:31.990 --> 00:13:34.780
Transform to swords, my Code!

00:13:37.210 --> 00:13:39.310
No matter how many times you try,
the result will be the same.

00:13:57.990 --> 00:13:59.200
In that case...

00:14:04.270 --> 00:14:05.400
I did it!

00:14:07.810 --> 00:14:08.900
No way...

00:14:13.710 --> 00:14:15.160
Koyomi...

00:14:24.730 --> 00:14:26.120
I did it!

00:14:32.760 --> 00:14:35.180
Koyomi... Why?

00:14:35.590 --> 00:14:38.210
I understand her Code.

00:14:38.210 --> 00:14:42.680
My body is shielded by a conglomeration
of several hundred ghostscripts.

00:14:43.060 --> 00:14:46.540
You have no way of touching
the Sorceress's Library.

00:14:46.890 --> 00:14:49.430
As long as we can't erase
the ghostscripts,

00:14:49.430 --> 00:14:51.450
we can't even get to the
Sorceress's Library.

00:14:51.770 --> 00:14:53.950
Even if we manage to get
rid of the ghostscripts,

00:14:53.950 --> 00:14:57.560
if we don't erase the Library,
you'll just keep adding more ghostscripts.

00:14:57.560 --> 00:15:00.200
You have no chance
of winning. Die.

00:15:00.810 --> 00:15:05.430
I can't lose here, but
I can't keep...

00:15:05.930 --> 00:15:07.720
Looks like you're having
a hard time.

00:15:13.070 --> 00:15:14.270
You're...

00:15:14.700 --> 00:15:16.150
So, you came.

00:15:16.150 --> 00:15:17.750
Who are you?

00:15:17.950 --> 00:15:21.210
I told you, I'm a good Santa.

00:15:23.130 --> 00:15:24.390
Are you okay?

00:15:24.390 --> 00:15:26.530
Y-Yes.

00:15:26.530 --> 00:15:28.570
Can you still construct Codes?

00:15:28.570 --> 00:15:31.180
One more at most...

00:15:31.750 --> 00:15:33.870
Come here for a second.

00:15:40.830 --> 00:15:44.480
I'll buy some time. So, you
two, work something out.

00:15:45.710 --> 00:15:49.000
You're the only one who can transform
the Sorceress's Library.

00:15:49.000 --> 00:15:51.130
Koyomi, you can do it, right?

00:15:57.730 --> 00:15:59.290
Do you think you can win?

00:16:01.000 --> 00:16:02.520
I wonder about that.

00:16:02.520 --> 00:16:06.030
Unlike those two, I'm perfectly
fine with being underhanded.

00:16:06.030 --> 00:16:08.650
That sounds fun. How
about you show me?

00:16:08.650 --> 00:16:10.430
I'm already doing it.

00:16:10.430 --> 00:16:13.240
Once a Modern-Day Mage
arrives on the scene,

00:16:13.240 --> 00:16:15.620
the Codes have already
been constructed.

00:16:15.620 --> 00:16:16.620
I see.

00:16:17.090 --> 00:16:22.200
The Christmas Shopper has already
entered these ghostscripts.

00:16:22.530 --> 00:16:24.490
You'd better hurry and
take off your armor.

00:16:25.160 --> 00:16:27.770
How about you die first?

00:16:33.720 --> 00:16:34.910
You're good.

00:16:35.250 --> 00:16:36.260
You too.

00:16:36.260 --> 00:16:38.840
But there's a tremendously
huge difference

00:16:38.840 --> 00:16:41.940
in the rate at which I can construct
Codes, Modern-Day Mage.

00:16:44.350 --> 00:16:46.300
You two, hurry up!

00:16:47.350 --> 00:16:49.020
We're doing this again.

00:16:49.020 --> 00:16:50.140
How?

00:16:50.420 --> 00:16:53.220
Once I hit him with a sword, a
hole will open in his armor.

00:16:53.220 --> 00:16:55.150
Pull the Code out from there.

00:16:55.150 --> 00:16:56.680
Got it!

00:17:05.800 --> 00:17:08.410
Transform to swords, my Code!

00:17:11.850 --> 00:17:13.090
Yumiko-chan!

00:17:13.350 --> 00:17:15.620
Not yet! Get the Code!

00:17:40.800 --> 00:17:41.740
Damned animal!

00:17:43.660 --> 00:17:45.160
Katamari!

00:17:52.750 --> 00:17:55.220
So we're really finished...

00:18:05.410 --> 00:18:08.360
Bring your friends
and come here.

00:18:09.940 --> 00:18:14.600
Bring your friends
and come here...

00:18:44.810 --> 00:18:46.270
No way!

00:18:47.810 --> 00:18:50.450
Father... Mother...

00:18:50.450 --> 00:18:52.280
Thank you.

00:18:52.970 --> 00:18:53.790
Koyomi!

00:18:54.070 --> 00:18:55.290
Right!

00:18:58.770 --> 00:19:00.820
S-Stop!

00:19:33.160 --> 00:19:35.500
"Kenjuro" is carved
into the shaft.

00:19:35.500 --> 00:19:39.730
One hundred years ago, he must have
finished off Guibarthez with this.

00:19:40.540 --> 00:19:43.350
He was a ghostscript, too.

00:19:43.350 --> 00:19:45.950
That's why he was so fixated
on the Sorceress's Library.

00:19:49.940 --> 00:19:51.950
This is pretty bad.

00:19:51.950 --> 00:19:54.780
I wonder if there's a vet open
on Christmas Eve...

00:20:01.500 --> 00:20:04.390
Let's do our best to
recover the staff.

00:20:05.670 --> 00:20:08.370
I don't even remember
her name anymore...

00:20:09.840 --> 00:20:12.770
But I'm sure I'll be able
to see her soon.

00:20:12.770 --> 00:20:16.870
I'll make sure to be good
friends with her then!

00:20:33.410 --> 00:20:36.130
Umm, I'm back...

00:20:36.130 --> 00:20:40.050
That's weird. The Code wasn't even
flowing through your body.

00:20:40.390 --> 00:20:45.260
Um, about how long was I
watching the ghostscript?

00:20:45.260 --> 00:20:46.470
Twenty-three seconds.

00:20:46.470 --> 00:20:48.200
Only a moment, I believe.

00:20:48.450 --> 00:20:49.690
I see.

00:20:49.690 --> 00:20:50.700
Huh?

00:20:50.700 --> 00:20:54.840
All the effects from the Christmas
Shopper's excess Code are gone.

00:20:54.840 --> 00:20:57.930
Koyomi, did you use a Code?

00:20:57.930 --> 00:21:02.150
Um... I kind of did, and
I kind of didn't...

00:21:02.150 --> 00:21:04.360
Oh, the password!

00:21:04.360 --> 00:21:06.930
It's okay. I don't need it anymore.

00:21:06.930 --> 00:21:09.170
But this is pretty weird...

00:21:09.170 --> 00:21:11.710
That's why I should have done it!

00:21:12.240 --> 00:21:14.570
I thought everyone would
have been busy,

00:21:14.570 --> 00:21:16.800
so I bought this for you.

00:21:17.360 --> 00:21:19.650
You thought right!

00:21:20.400 --> 00:21:22.630
Time to eat!

00:21:23.020 --> 00:21:24.640
Thanks...

00:21:25.280 --> 00:21:27.680
Koyomi, you have some, too.

00:21:29.440 --> 00:21:32.530
Yumiko-chan, you're not
using a knife and fork!

00:21:33.380 --> 00:21:36.650
Morishita, I think you're teasing
her a bit too much.

00:21:36.650 --> 00:21:40.340
Y-You're right. Sorry.

00:21:41.270 --> 00:21:44.660
As your punishment, take
some to Soshiro too.

00:21:47.540 --> 00:21:49.450
He's sure eating well!

00:21:52.520 --> 00:21:55.130
Of course a cat's going to eat.

00:21:56.750 --> 00:21:59.480
Katamari, you've sure
gotten bigger.

00:22:00.290 --> 00:22:03.260
Huh, how do you know his name?

00:22:03.260 --> 00:22:06.400
Because he'll ball up and not move, right?

00:22:06.400 --> 00:22:08.230
It's a cute name.

00:22:08.230 --> 00:22:10.440
Did I tell you that?

00:22:10.440 --> 00:22:12.540
Right, Katamari?

00:23:46.400 --> 00:23:50.020
The differences between the
girl mage and myself...

00:23:50.020 --> 00:23:52.700
They're not just physical.

00:23:52.700 --> 00:23:56.660
In order to get a magic
item like Kerykeion,

00:23:56.660 --> 00:23:59.490
the girl heads to the streets of Shibuya.

00:24:04.530 --> 00:24:07.050
"Spell = Code"?

00:24:07.280 --> 00:24:10.140
Hi! Dying from the heat?

00:24:07.650 --> 00:24:14.570
Shinbashi?

00:24:10.140 --> 00:24:11.470
Morishita Koyomi here.

00:24:11.470 --> 00:24:13.850
Hi, Anehara Misa here.

00:24:13.850 --> 00:24:16.310
Let's have fun studying today.

00:24:16.310 --> 00:24:18.340
Today is about spells?

00:24:18.340 --> 00:24:22.410
Um... Misa-san, Misa-san! Didn't
we go over this before?

00:24:22.410 --> 00:24:23.650
You're right.

00:24:23.650 --> 00:24:25.500
The first time we
did this segment,

00:24:25.500 --> 00:24:28.860
we went over it a bit when
we talked about magic.

00:24:28.860 --> 00:24:32.080
So, Koyomi, you know
all about it, huh?

00:24:32.080 --> 00:24:33.770
We're doing a review?!

00:24:33.770 --> 00:24:36.080
Yep, review is important.

00:24:36.080 --> 00:24:39.750
Anyway, Koyomi-san,
what is a spell?

00:24:39.750 --> 00:24:42.770
U-Um... Spells are kind of like

00:24:42.770 --> 00:24:46.830
what Yumiko-chan says before
she uses magic, right?

00:24:46.830 --> 00:24:48.480
What was it...

00:24:48.480 --> 00:24:51.850
If you're the one... Um...

00:24:51.850 --> 00:24:55.570
What time... Time...
What time is it...

00:24:56.320 --> 00:24:59.350
Jeez, you don't know
at all! Pout! Pout!

00:24:59.350 --> 00:25:00.730
I-I'm sorry.

00:25:00.730 --> 00:25:03.840
Also, the incantation itself
has no real meaning.

00:25:03.840 --> 00:25:06.330
It's just something that
helps you concentrate.

00:25:06.330 --> 00:25:10.410
Oh, you said that in the second
episode of the anime!

00:25:10.410 --> 00:25:11.560
That's right.

00:25:11.560 --> 00:25:13.140
As I said back then,

00:25:13.140 --> 00:25:16.600
magic doesn't happen because
of the incantation.

00:25:16.600 --> 00:25:20.150
That might be the difference in our magic,
compared to those in other manga and anime.

00:25:20.150 --> 00:25:21.780
I see.

00:25:21.780 --> 00:25:28.500
So in the world of <i>Yoku Wakaru Gendai
Mahou</i>, what would you call a spell?

00:25:28.500 --> 00:25:31.100
Um... Um...

00:25:31.100 --> 00:25:33.050
A-A Code!

00:25:33.050 --> 00:25:38.980
That's right! In this world,
spells are called Codes.

00:25:38.980 --> 00:25:43.060
And regarding Codes... Oh,
I guess we're out of time.

00:25:43.060 --> 00:25:44.910
That's all we have for
today's lecture!

00:25:44.910 --> 00:25:47.100
We'll continue next time.

00:25:47.100 --> 00:25:48.260
Okay!

00:25:48.260 --> 00:25:50.200
Here's the summary for today!

00:25:50.200 --> 00:25:54.350
1. Magic doesn't occur just
because you chant a spell.

00:25:54.350 --> 00:25:58.750
2. Magical incantations are just
things that help you focus,

00:25:58.750 --> 00:26:01.750
making it easier to activate
the magic.

00:26:01.750 --> 00:26:04.550
3. Spells are called Codes.

00:26:04.550 --> 00:26:06.740
Did you get all that?

00:26:06.740 --> 00:26:09.910
OK, everyone, see you next week!

00:26:08.510 --> 00:26:09.910
Bye!
